      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "DISTRIBUTED CACHE",
      "fontSize": 59.03999023437499,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "DISTRIBUTED CACHE",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VfPTlXFwVDpSFAlzXKido",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 833.5999755859377,
      "y": 492.699981689453,
      "width": 1303.9329833984375,
      "height": 443.80004882812483,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b17",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 529500873,
      "version": 1816,
      "versionNonce": 1797147337,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788467542229,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> Cache Aside: Seperate Cache. If there is a cache hit, \nget it from the cache. If there is a cache miss, get it from the DB. Used here.\nand then write to Cache. Most frequent type of caching.\n-> Write Through: Write to Cache which writes to DB. Dual write problem,\nif Write fails in DB then we need retry logic, error handling.\nCannot give perfect consistency in Distributed Systems.\n-> Write Behind: Write to cache and read from cache. \nCache async writes flush to DB. Use when we need high throughput.\nData loss could be happen\n-> Read Through: Servers check cache and if there is a miss, cache reads from DB\nand returns to server.",
      "fontSize": 32.276367187499986,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> Cache Aside: Seperate Cache. If there is a cache hit, \nget it from the cache. If there is a cache miss, get it from the DB. Used here.\nand then write to Cache. Most frequent type of caching.\n-> Write Through: Write to Cache which writes to DB. Dual write problem,\nif Write fails in DB then we need retry logic, error handling.\nCannot give perfect consistency in Distributed Systems.\n-> Write Behind: Write to cache and read from cache. \nCache async writes flush to DB. Use when we need high throughput.\nData loss could be happen\n-> Read Through: Servers check cache and if there is a miss, cache reads from DB\nand returns to server.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vqsCZQSRiFRfi_Q5k0VvS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -361.911142985026,
      "y": 488.1856177193778,
      "width": 1070.3274431080715,
      "height": 229.99993896484372,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b18",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1415354951,
      "version": 865,
      "versionNonce": 1459360425,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788467454854,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Cache Eviction Policies\n\nLRU - Evict items that have not been used recently. Most Common.\nLFU - Evict items that are used least often, even if accessed recently.\nFIFO - Evict the oldest item first. Simple but rarely the right choice.\nTTL - Each item expires after a set time. Great for API responses.",
      "fontSize": 30.66665852864573,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Cache Eviction Policies\n\nLRU - Evict items that have not been used recently. Most Common.\nLFU - Evict items that are used least often, even if accessed recently.\nFIFO - Evict the oldest item first. Simple but rarely the right choice.\nTTL - Each item expires after a set time. Great for API responses.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8vWedLDEACXuH8_h7G4ng",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -370.71125284830725,
      "y": 744.1854040963309,
      "width": 1431.8075404374272,
      "height": 367.00018310546864,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1A",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 37192009,
      "version": 1241,
      "versionNonce": 336145479,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788467337956,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Common Issues\n\nCache Stampede - When a lot of requests come in and there are a lot of cache misses. \nCan be avoided by using Single Flight and Cache worming, \nwhere we refresh popular set of keys when they are about to expire.\n\nCache Inconsistency - Cache and DB returns different data.\nCan be prevented by Invalidating on Write, create short TTLs, accepting eventual inconsistency.\n\nHot keys - When one key is too popular that it burdens the caching server. \nCan be avoided by replicating the hot key, add a fallback cache to the servers with a cache inside the server.",
      "fontSize": 26.690922407670428,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Common Issues\n\nCache Stampede - When a lot of requests come in and there are a lot of cache misses. \nCan be avoided by using Single Flight and Cache worming, \nwhere we refresh popular set of keys when they are about to expire.\n\nCache Inconsistency - Cache and DB returns different data.\nCan be prevented by Invalidating on Write, create short TTLs, accepting eventual inconsistency.\n\nHot keys - When one key is too popular that it burdens the caching server. \nCan be avoided by replicating the hot key, add a fallback cache to the servers with a cache inside the server.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
